# Rules for Cursor & Copilot in epson-print-server

- Target OS: Windows 11 (x64)
- Target Device: Epson EcoTank L3110 All-in-One USB
- Languages: Python 3.10+ (Backend & Hardware Engine) and Node.js (Web UI & Gateway).
- Strict Rule: Absolutely NO C# or .NET code, assemblies, or tools.
- Windows Subsystems:
  - Scanner: Windows Image Acquisition (WIA 2.0 COM) via Python `win32com.client`.
  - Printer: Windows Print Spooler (`winspool.drv`) via `win32print` or `win32api.ShellExecute("printto", ...)`.
  - AirPrint: RFC 8010/8011 IPP 2.0 binary parser on TCP port 631 + mDNS via `zeroconf`.
- Python COM Safety: Always call `pythoncom.CoInitialize()` and `pythoncom.CoUninitialize()` when invoking WIA.
